IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha-types`
IMPORT `ha-pay`
IMPORT `ha-annual`
IMPORT `ha-public`
IMPORT `ha-leave`
IMPORT `ha-enforcement`
IMPORT `ha-goal`

-- Holidays Act 2003 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from
-- ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_129.txt, not from the code.
-- Amounts are made up; the Act fixes none of its own except the 8%, the
-- penalty maxima, and the day counts.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

-- Weekly pay determinable under s 8(1): ordinary week, regular incentives,
-- regular overtime.
GIVEN ordinary IS A NUMBER, incentive IS A NUMBER, overtime IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Weekly pay facts`
`weekly` ordinary incentive overtime MEANS
    `Weekly pay facts` OF TRUE, ordinary, incentive, overtime, NOTHING, 0, 0, NOTHING

-- Relevant daily pay determinable, not varying.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Daily pay facts`
`daily` amount MEANS
    `Daily pay facts` OF TRUE, amount, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of absence`, days IS A NUMBER, agreed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Absence
`absence` kind days agreed MEANS Absence OF kind, days, agreed

`Monday to Friday` MEANS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Calendar inputs`
`weekday calendar` y MEANS `Calendar inputs` OF y, Date 20 6 y, Date 20 1 y, `Monday to Friday`

GIVEN start IS A DATE
GIVETH A Service
`service from` start MEANS Service OF start, NOTHING, FALSE

-- A spell of leave of kind k from day d, for an employee who started on s:
-- days asked, days left, whose sickness, bereavements.
GIVEN k IS A `Leave kind`, d IS A DATE, s IS A DATE, asked IS A NUMBER, left IS A NUMBER, w IS A `Whose sickness`, bs IS A LIST OF Bereavement
GIVETH A Leave
`leave` k d s asked left w bs MEANS
    Leave OF k, d, `service from` s, asked, left, FALSE, w, bs, (`Family violence facts` OF TRUE, FALSE), `daily` 200, 0, FALSE

`no bereavements` MEANS LIST `(b) the death of another person, if the employer does not accept it`

-- A public holiday: otherwise a working day, worked, the s 50 inputs.
GIVEN otherwise IS A BOOLEAN, worked IS A BOOLEAN, portion IS A NUMBER, penal IS A NUMBER, rdp IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Public holiday worked or not`
`public holiday` otherwise worked portion penal rdp MEANS
    `Public holiday worked or not` OF Date 25 4 2025, otherwise, worked, worked, `any other reason`, FALSE, `not on call`, `daily` 200, portion, penal, rdp

`a full record` MEANS
    `Holiday and leave record` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

§§ `Goal 1 — the pay measures`

-- s 10
#ASSERT `the cash value of board or lodgings counted` NOTHING EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the cash value of board or lodgings counted` (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 50, FALSE, FALSE)) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the cash value of board or lodgings counted` (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 50, TRUE, FALSE)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the cash value of board or lodgings counted` (JUST (`Board or lodgings` OF 50, FALSE, TRUE)) EQUALS 0

-- s 14, s 10A: wages 1000 + overtime 200 + HCS s 14 50 + first week comp 80
-- count; discretionary 300, super 30, ACC weekly 400, HCS s 19 20, s 28B
-- payout 100 do not: 1330.
#ASSERT `the gross earnings in` (LIST (Payment OF `(a)(i) salary or wages`, 1000), (Payment OF `(a)(v) a payment for overtime`, 200), (Payment OF `(b)(i) a discretionary payment`, 300), (Payment OF `(c)(iii) an employer contribution to a superannuation scheme`, 30), (Payment OF `(b)(ii) weekly compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 2001`, 400), (Payment OF `s 10A(a) a payment under s 14 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016`, 50), (Payment OF `s 10A(b) a payment under s 19 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016`, 20), (Payment OF `(c)(iv) a payment for annual holidays paid out under s 28B`, 100), (Payment OF `(a)(vii) first week compensation under s 97 of the Accident Compensation Act 2001`, 80)) EQUALS 1330
#ASSERT `the gross earnings in` (LIST (Payment OF `(a)(iii) pay for a holiday or leave taken in the period`, 400), (Payment OF `(c)(i) a reimbursement of actual costs`, 60), (Payment OF `(c)(ii) a reimbursement of a reasonably assessed amount of costs`, 25), (Payment OF `(b)(iii) a payment for absence on volunteers leave`, 150)) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the gross earnings in` (LIST (Payment OF `(a)(ii) an allowance, other than a non-taxable reimbursement of actual costs`, 70), (Payment OF `(a)(iv) a productivity or incentive-based payment`, 30), (Payment OF `(a)(vi) the cash value of board or lodgings agreed or determined under s 10`, 40)) EQUALS 140

-- s 8(1): 1000 + 100 + 50 + board 40 = 1190
